    17	Geometry enters `xRIR.forward` through the ViT views `(loc − depth_coord)/5` and the sinusoidal embedding of raw xyz. Active yaw by k columns (W = 512): `depth' = Rz(2πk/W)·roll(depth, k)`, `src' = Rz·src`, `ref_locs' = Rz·ref_locs`; reference audio and target unchanged (`tools/yaw_rotation.rotate_scene_yaw`, oracle-tested in exp_03). Condition **P** pins the direct-path alignment at k = 0 (`tools/yaw_rotation.fixed_alignment`) so only the geometry branches see the rotation — the analogue of FLAC's `--rotate-deg`, which rotates the conditioning and leaves the audio untouched. exp_03 measured E (end-to-end alignment) = P to 2e-5 **at K = 8**; E is not run here. The model outputs a log-magnitude `out` `[F=63, T=310]`; the magnitude is `M = exp(out) − 1e-8` (built on the inference device, then moved to CPU exactly as exp_03's `acoustic_metrics_batch` does) and the waveform is Griffin-Lim on CPU (`tools/per_sample_metrics.griffin_lim_seeded`, 32 iterations, phase seeded by `sample_seed(gl_seed, query)`), 9 579 samples zero-padded to 9 600.
